CONTEXT
    darwin/amd64 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vinod-rightmo/inux/HEAD/bin/adf-darwin-amd64
    darwin/arm64 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vinod-rightmo/inux/HEAD/bin/adf-darwin-arm64
    linux/amd64 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vinod-rightmo/inux/HEAD/bin/adf-linux-amd64
    linux/arm64 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vinod-rightmo/inux/HEAD/bin/adf-linux-arm64
    windows/amd64 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/vinod-rightmo/inux/HEAD/bin/adf-windows-amd64.exe
AS converter_downloads

DO Select the exact download URL from @converter_downloads for @platform.os and
    @platform.arch. If @options.repository is non-NULL, replace vinod-rightmo/inux
    in the URL with that repository. If @options.adf_ref is non-NULL, replace the
    HEAD path segment with that branch or commit, preserving it as a URL path.
    Return an object with url. AS converter_package

PRINT "Step 2 of 3: Set up Markdown converter (adf)."

DO Download @converter_package.url and install at @host.adf as one bounded
    transaction under @install_rules. Save the HTTP response bytes directly to a
    file in a unique private temporary directory and require a successful HTTP
    status; never print or text-decode the binary. Set executable permissions and
    run the downloaded binary with a small UTF-8 Markdown fixture and a separate
    .adf output file. Require valid ADF representing the fixture and an unchanged
    input. Compare the verified binary bytes with any installed copy; retain an
    identical copy or replace it at @host.adf. Preserve a working installation on
    failure. Clean only this transaction's temporary files on success or failure.
    Return an object with path, ready TRUE, and Boolean updated. AS converter

PRINT Report the verified converter path @converter.path and whether it was updated.
